\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.4}{\ignorespaces Lifting the $2\text  {-}D${} fitted model into $p\text  {-}D${}. Two projections of the $p\text  {-}D${} fitted model overlaying the data are shown in b, c.~The fit is reasonably tight with the data in one cluster (top one in b), but slightly less so in the other cluster probably because it is \(3\text  {-}D\). Notice also that, in the $2\text  {-}D${} layout the two clusters have internal gaps which creates a model with some holes. This lacy pattern happens regardless of the hyper-parameter choice, but this doesn't severely impact the $p\text  {-}D${} model representation.}}{10}{figure.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
