\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.8}{\ignorespaces Assessing which of the 6 NLDR layouts (a-f) on the 2NC7 data is the better representation using HBE for varying binwidth (\(a_1\)) and average bin count (\(\bar  {n}_h\)). Color represents NLDR layout. Layout d is universally poor. Layouts a, b, e that show two close clusters are universally suboptimal. Layout b with little separation performs well at tiny binwidth (where most points are in their own bin) and poorly as binwidth increases. Layout e has small separation with oddly shaped clusters. Layout a is the best choice. Comparison of scaled evaluation metrics (rRTA, rSC, rGS, rARNX, and HBE using \(a_1=0.05\)) for the six NLDR layouts computed on the 2NC7 data using a parallel coordinate plot. Color of the line indicates NLDR layout. RTA, SC, GS, and ARNX is reversed so that lower is best.}}{17}{figure.caption.16}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig-toy-rmse}{{2.8}{17}{Assessing which of the 6 NLDR layouts (a-f) on the 2NC7 data is the better representation using HBE for varying binwidth (\(a_1\)) and average bin count (\(\bar {n}_h\)). Color represents NLDR layout. Layout d is universally poor. Layouts a, b, e that show two close clusters are universally suboptimal. Layout b with little separation performs well at tiny binwidth (where most points are in their own bin) and poorly as binwidth increases. Layout e has small separation with oddly shaped clusters. Layout a is the best choice. Comparison of scaled evaluation metrics (rRTA, rSC, rGS, rARNX, and HBE using \(a_1=0.05\)) for the six NLDR layouts computed on the 2NC7 data using a parallel coordinate plot. Color of the line indicates NLDR layout. RTA, SC, GS, and ARNX is reversed so that lower is best}{figure.caption.16}{}}
